## WordPress Best Practices Checklist

Every WordPress component must include:

### ✅ Accessibility (WCAG 2.2 AA)
- Proper ARIA attributes
- Keyboard navigation
- Screen reader compatibility
- Semantic HTML structure
- Focus management

### ✅ Performance
- Lazy loading for scripts/styles
- Efficient asset enqueuing
- Minimal DOM manipulation
- Optimized queries (if applicable)
- No render-blocking resources

### ✅ Security
- Escaping all output (`esc_html`, `esc_attr`, `wp_kses`)
- Sanitizing all input
- Nonce verification for forms
- Capability checks for restricted actions
- No SQL injection vulnerabilities

### ✅ Internationalization (i18n)
- All strings wrapped in `__()` or `_e()`
- Proper text domain
- Translation-ready
- RTL support considerations

### ✅ Block Editor Integration
- Follows Block API v3
- Proper block.json configuration
- Editor and frontend styles separated
- Block validation working correctly
- No console errors in editor

### ✅ FSE Compatibility
- Works with block themes
- Integrates with theme.json
- Supports global styles
- Compatible with template parts
- Pattern-ready structure

### ✅ Code Quality
- Follows WordPress Coding Standards
- PHPStan level 5+ compliance
- ESLint passing
- Proper documentation
- No deprecated functions

